description:
Decide which plugins a host may load, which ones receive each event, and when to disable a misbehaving one (lesson 6.03):

```cpp
struct Manifest { std::string name; int apiMajor; int apiMinor; std::vector<std::string> events; };

class PluginHost
{
public:
    PluginHost(int apiMajor, int apiMinor);
    bool load(const Manifest& m);
    std::vector<std::string> route(const std::string& event) const;
    bool reportTimeout(const std::string& plugin, std::uint64_t now);
    std::vector<std::string> enabled() const;
};
```

- **load** accepts a plugin only if its API major equals the host's and its API minor is **not newer** than the host's, and no plugin of the same name (ignoring case) is loaded. It returns whether it was loaded.
- **route** lists the enabled plugins subscribed to `event`, in the order they were loaded. The event name `*` in a manifest subscribes to everything.
- **reportTimeout** records a timeout for a plugin; if it has had **3 timeouts within 60 seconds** (times `now - 60` to `now`), it is disabled. It returns true if this report disabled it. Disabled plugins are never routed to, and reports about them or unknown plugins return false.
- **enabled** lists enabled plugin names in load order.

